    ["plugin_files",
    ".P",
    "LightWave Plug-in",
    "2.5",
    "A P file is a pickle file created by pickle, a Python module used for converting Python objects to a byte representation for storage on disk or transfer over a network. It allows for objects to be conveniently stored or transmitted without first having to convert the data to another format. P files can be unpickled and loaded back into program memory during runtime. You will most likely only encounter Python pickle P files if you use the pickle module to convert a Python object hierarchy into a byte stream. This may also be referred to as serialization. The Python scripting language is typically used for programming web applications and dynamic web content. NOTE: P files may also be saved as.PICKLE files. You can use Python pickle (multiplatform) to read the data serialized in a P file. For more detailed instructions, refer to pickles documentation. Windows Python pickle. Mac Python pickle. Linux Python pickleFree. A P file is a source code file written in the Pascal programming language. It contains Pascal source code that can be edited with a Pascal development program or a basic text editor. P files can be compiled into executable programs using a Pascal compiler such as Turbo Pascal. Pascal was originally developed in the late 1960s and published in 1970 by Niklaus Wirth. It is a procedural language that has led to several different variants such as Super Pascal and Pascal Sol. Object Pascal is also an extension of Pascal that was developed in 1985 and designed for object-oriented programming at Apple Computer. P files are one of several files used to store Pascal source code, along with the more common.PAS file. Windows. Pascal. Borland Turbo Pascal. Irie Tools Irie Pascal Mac. Pascal. Bare Bones BBEdit. MacroMates TextMateFree. Plugin file used by LightWave 3D, a 3D modeling and rendering application for animations and still images; stores data and procedures used for extending the softwares functionality; often used for auto-generating custom 3D objects and modifying existing object properties. Windows NewTek LightWave 3D. Mac NewTek LightWave 3D. A P file is an image created by Ashton-Tate Applause, a graphics program for MS-DOS used to create business presentations. It contains vector image data for a presentation graphic, which may include text, 3D shapes, and clipart images. P files are primarily used to store business presentations, such as quarterly reviews and strategies. Ashton-Tate was a software company in the 1980s that was sold to Borland Software Corporation in 1991. One of Ashton-Tates software offerings was Draw Applause, later renamed Applause (released in 1998), which was a slide-making presentation program. Applause was discontinued in 1991 when Ashton-Tate was absorbed by Borland. You can open P files with Ashton-Tate Applause by selecting File → Open.. Borland discontinued Applause when it acquired Ashton-Tate in 1991, but the program is still available for download and can only be run in MS-DOS. Windows Ashton-Tate Applause —  (Discontinued).",
    "Windows Python pickle. Mac Python pickle. Linux Python pickle. Windows. Pascal. Borland Turbo Pascal. Irie Tools Irie Pascal. Mac. Pascal. Bare Bones BBEdit. MacroMates TextMate. Windows NewTek LightWave 3D. Mac NewTek LightWave 3D. Windows Ashton-Tate Applause —  (Discontinued).",
    "?"],
    ["plugin_files",
    ".M2P",
    "Maxthon 2 Browser Plugin File",
    "2.5",
    "Video container format that supports MPEG-2 audio and video compression; similar to an MPEG-1 file, but also supports interlaced video and more audio channels; commonly used for streaming digital video. NOTE: M2P files are generally used for streaming media. Standard MPEG-2 video files typically have an.MPG extension, while standard MPEG-2 audio files usually have an.MP2 extension. Windows Roxio Creator NXT Pro 9. Microsoft Windows Media Player Included with OS. Media Player Classic. VideoLAN VLC media player. Elecard MPEG Player. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Roxio Toast 20. Squared 5 MPEG Streamclip. iOS PentaLoop PlayerXtreme Media Player. Plugin installation pack for the Maxthon Web browser; includes a compressed add-on for Maxthon that provides additional features and capabilities within the program. M2P files are essentially.ZIP files renamed with a .m2p extension. They can be installed by double-clicking the file or dragging the file into an open Maxthon browser window. Windows MaxthonFree.",
    "Windows Roxio Creator NXT Pro 9. Microsoft Windows Media Player Included with OS. Media Player Classic. VideoLAN VLC media player. Elecard MPEG Player. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Roxio Toast 20. Squared 5 MPEG Streamclip. iOS PentaLoop PlayerXtreme Media Player. Windows Maxthon.",
    "?"],
    ["plugin_files",
    ".Q8R",
    "Flood Photoshop Plug-in",
    "2.5",
    "Photoshop plug-in developed by Flaming Pear Software; used for creating 3D watery images with realistic reflections; must reside in the Plug-ins folder within the application folder to work. Windows Adobe Photoshop 2023. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023.",
    "Windows Adobe Photoshop 2023. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023.",
    "?"],
    ["plugin_files",
    ".IADCOMPONENT",
    "iAd Producer Plugin Component File",
    "2.5",
    "Plugin data file referenced by iAd Producer, an application used to create rich interactive content for iOS advertisements; describes components, such as buttons, sliders, and labels. The IADCOMPONENT file is contains component information such as height, width, padding, text, and background appearance. The components are utilized by.IADPLUG plugins and are stored in IADPLUG files, along with.IADCLASS,.JS,.JSON,.CSS, and.PNG files. IADPLUG files that come with iAd Producer are located in the following directory: /​Applications/​iAd Producer/​Contents/​iAdPlugins/​. Mac Apple iAd Producer —  (Discontinued).",
    "Mac Apple iAd Producer —  (Discontinued).",
    "?"],
    ["plugin_files",
    ".LRMODULE",
    "Adobe Lightroom Module",
    "2.5",
    "An LRMODULE file is a module used by Adobe Lightroom, a professional photo editing and organization application, or Lightroom Classic. Each LRMODULE file contains data used to load one or more Lightroom features, such as the ability to import and export photos. LRMODULE files are not meant to be manually opened by users. In macOS, LRMODULE files are stored in Lightrooms PlugIns directory. In Windows, they are stored in Lightrooms Adobe Lightroom CC directory. Version 5 of Lightroom contains the following LRMODULE files: AdobeHeadlights.lrmodule AdobeHelpClient.lrmodule Develop.lrmodule Export.lrmodule ExternalEdit.lrmodule Import.lrmodule Organize.lrmodule Watermark.lrmodule. LRMODULE files are not meant to be opened. To access the feature(s) an LRMODULE file contains, open Adobe Lightroom or Adobe Lightroom Classic and use that feature. Windows Adobe Lightroom. Adobe Lightroom Classic. Mac Adobe Lightroom. Adobe Lightroom Classic.",
    "Windows Adobe Lightroom. Adobe Lightroom Classic. Mac Adobe Lightroom. Adobe Lightroom Classic.",
    "?"],
    ["plugin_files",
    ".XCODEPLUGIN",
    "Xcode Plug-in",
    "2.5",
    "Plugin used by Apple Xcode, an IDE used to create iOS and OS X apps; contains data referenced by Xcode to extend the applications capabilities, such as a Clean Up Whitespace menu item that removes unnecessary end of line white space from text files. XCODEPLUGIN files should be installed in the ~/​Library/​Application Support/​Developer/​Shared/​Xcode/​Plug-ins directory. If the pathway does not exist, create it. Restart Xcode after installation to see the plugin functions appear in the application. NOTE: The xcodeplugin extension was used by Xcode 3, but was replaced with the.DVTPLUGIN file in Xcode 4. Mac Apple XcodeFree.",
    "Mac Apple Xcode.",
    "?"],
    ["plugin_files",
    ".CST",
    "Gary Gadget Plug-in",
    "2.5",
    "Page layout file created by Manga Studio, a program used for creating comic books; saves the storyline for the comic book and can include multiple chapters, multiple pages (.CPG files) per chapter, and layouts for each page; used for specifying the structure of the comic book. Manga Studio became Clip Studio Paint in 2015. It is also known as ComicStudio in Japan. Windows CELSYS Clip Studio Paint Pro. Mac CELSYS Clip Studio Paint Pro. Cast file created by Adobe Director, a movie creation program originally developed by Macromedia; stores properties for generating the video output; allows a cast to be reused for multiple videos. CST files contain external casts, which are fully delinked from the target movie. Internal casts, on the other hand, cannot be delinked from the movie and may only be used for the movie they are linked to. Since Adobe Director has been replaced by Adobe Flash, CST files are not commonly used anymore. Windows Adobe Director —  (Discontinued). Trial Mac Adobe Director —  (Discontinued). Trial. Settings file created by Canvas, a technical illustration program; contains application keyboard shortcuts used to access program functions; allows users to save custom workspace preferences. CST files can include key combinations for selections of menus, tools, inks, pens, and fonts. The default custom set is saved in the DefaultKeyboard.cst file, which is located in the /​Extras/​ directory of the Canvas installation. Windows Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. Plugin file used by Gary Gadget: Building Cars, a car designing, building, and driving game for children; adds features to the game such as car parts or bonus games. CST plugin files are available to download from the Gary Gadget: Building Cars website. When the download is complete, place the CST file(s) in the Gary Gadget/​Building Cars/​Plugins directory of the game installation location. If the Plugins folder doesnt exist, you will need to create it. After placing the file(s) in the folder, restart the game and the plugin(s) will be available. NOTE: The Viva Media Gary Gadget: Building Cars program is no longer available for download. Windows Viva Media Gary Gadget: Building Cars Mac Viva Media Gary Gadget: Building Cars. A CST file is a script used by a visual novel developed using the CatSystem2 game engine. It contains data used to load and play a visual novel scene. This includes metadata and commands used to display text, play audio, and show sprites and animations. CatSystem2 is a visual novel game engine developed by Windmill. It is the successor to the original CatSystem, which was developed by Cat Works Team. Various developers use CatSystem2 to create visual novels. For example, Frontwings Grisaia series and Azarashi Softwares Amakano series both use CatSystem2. Games developed using CatSystem2 include scripts saved as CST files. Each script contains commands used to load and play a particular scene. For this reason, you may also see CST files referred to as CatSystem2 scenes or CST scenes. You can open a CST file with CatSceneEditor (multiplatform) or TriggersTools.CatSystem2 (multiplatform). Doing so will allow you to edit the data the CST file contains. Windows CatSceneEditor. TriggersTools.CatSystem2. Mac CatSceneEditor. TriggersTools.CatSystem2. Linux CatSceneEditor. TriggersTools.CatSystem2Free. Template for creating a new ContentServ document; may be used by an Enterprise Marketing Management Solutions (EMMS) project for managing marketing, sales, and communication processes. ContentServ templates include CSTags, which define content that is replaced by output from the template engine when the document is accessed. Windows ContentServ CS EMMS Suite (requires Apache Web Server) Linux ContentServ CS EMMS Suite (requires Apache Web Server).",
    "Windows CELSYS Clip Studio Paint Pro. Mac CELSYS Clip Studio Paint Pro. Windows Adobe Director —  (Discontinued). Trial. Mac Adobe Director —  (Discontinued). Trial. Windows Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. Windows Viva Media Gary Gadget: Building Cars. Mac Viva Media Gary Gadget: Building Cars. Windows CatSceneEditor. TriggersTools.CatSystem2. Mac CatSceneEditor. TriggersTools.CatSystem2. Linux CatSceneEditor. TriggersTools.CatSystem2. Windows ContentServ CS EMMS Suite (requires Apache Web Server). Linux ContentServ CS EMMS Suite (requires Apache Web Server).",
    "?"],
    ["plugin_files",
    ".PLX",
    "32-bit Linux IDA Plugin Module",
    "2.5",
    "Executable program written in the Perl programming language; often used for Web applications that are run on a Web server, but may be run on any system that includes a Perl interpreter. Perl scripts can be run on Windows IIS systems using Perl for ISAPI (Internet Server Application Programming Interface) or with ActivePerl. The standard way of naming Perl files is.PM for Perl modules,.PL for Perl libraries, and PLX for executable Perl scripts. Windows ActiveState ActivePerl. Microsoft IIS with PerlIS. Mac ActiveState ActivePerl. Bare Bones BBEdit. Linux ActiveState ActivePerlFree. 32-bit Linux plugin module used by IDA (The Interactive Disassembler), a tool that allows users to disassemble executable files into low-level assembly language code; contains a plugin written in C++ that extends the capabilities of the IDA tool. The PLX files are loadable libraries, similar to.DLL, that extend IDAs functionality. The PLX plugin should be placed in the /​plugin/​plx/​ directory. NOTE: Each IDA plugin uses a different extension depending on its operating system type. The.PLW extension is used for Windows 32-bit, the.P64 extension is used by Windows 64-bit, and the.PLX64 extension is used by Linux 64-bit plugins. Linux Hex-Rays IDA.",
    "Windows ActiveState ActivePerl. Microsoft IIS with PerlIS. Mac ActiveState ActivePerl. Bare Bones BBEdit. Linux ActiveState ActivePerl. Linux Hex-Rays IDA.",
    "?"],
